                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Got this one out of nostalgia for the Wii release. Looking back, it's just... not that good, I guess? It still might be worth checking out, especially given its very reasonable price, but there are just better games out there. Linux users beware: you need to install a helper package with protontricks to get it working, but do NOT delete the deps directory like certain guides instruct to do (see https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1664621832).\n\nIn a sense this is the opposite of a regular shmup's core design idea: your movement is restricted to a single dimension but you can aim freely. Practically speaking, this means that dodging is generally more rigid (and extra annoying when there's a bullet flying right along the movement line) and aiming is largely separate from your movement. This is occasionally mixed up a little by adding an environmental obstacle or two or giving you a temporary powerup, but overall there isn't a whole lot of variety and the pace is rather slow for how minimalistic the challenge is, both in stages and boss fights.\n\nMusic and visuals are nice as expected, but in the end you'll probably be better served by playing something else; I personally just got bored midway through the game. It's an okay if unique idea with okay execution, so consider this a pretty neutral review.",
